# fixedbugs, defect 2364, lane p239-land-a, 2026-11-09 (panel 239's R4; the
# compiler-engineer's `nested`).
#
# This module spells `outer.Outer` alone, and `Outer` holds an `In`, which
# `fixedbugs-2364-outer.h` lays out wide where the macro of
# `fixedbugs-2364-wide.h` is read before it. Before the repair the build was
# refused, *`In.a` is `long long`*, false of the header as module `outer`
# reads it; now `Outer`'s layout, which holds `In`'s, is read as its own
# module reads it.
use fixedbugs2364/defines_wide
use fixedbugs2364/outer

function main()
    p = defines_wide.make(v: 4)
    o = outer.make(v: 3)
    print(p.w)
    print(o.c)
    print(o.r.a)
    print(o.r.b)
